- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests`

**How to implement.** A kit open elsewhere is offered read-only (001 §E 'a .oc/lock … warns across processes and machines, with an open read-only choice'; the S4.3 brief: a foreign lock offers 'Open read-only'; .spec-md §10.5: the opposing pair Open read-only / Cancel shares one row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; §3.12: a read-only open writes nothing). (1) In `Program.fs`' `LauncherWindow`, when the open of a picked folder (step 154) answers `Error (KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr holder))`, no window opens; `launcherKitErrorText` reads `The kit is open elsewhere: <holder.describe>.` (step 129), and under it one horizontal row holds `Open read-only` (`ConstructorUiId.launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton`, background `MaterialsWindowView.positiveBackground`) and, 12 px to its right, `Cancel` (`ConstructorUiId.launcherCancelKitOpenButton`, background `MaterialsWindowView.negativeBackground`; both colours public since step 107), each carrying its id as `Name` and `AutomationId`. `Open read-only` calls step 154's local function for the same folder and mode with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, and on success removes the text and the row. `Cancel` removes them and opens nothing. Every other error keeps step 154's text with no row. A window opened read-only works in the read-only context, so each kit write it asks answers `KitReadOnlyErr` in its `kitStatus` (step 152); S5.3 adds the title marker and disables those messages. (2) `UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton` (`"LauncherOpenKitReadOnlyButton"`) and `launcherCancelKitOpenButton` (`"LauncherCancelKitOpenButton"`), each with a one-line doc. (3) Tests, in `LauncherTests`, each holding the picked kit open through an `openKitAt` of its own, as a second window would, and closing it at the end, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing`: clicking Main shows the holder's text naming this process and both buttons with equal tops, `Cancel` to the right of `Open read-only` with a gap; clicking `Open read-only` opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow` and removes the row, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes, the other holder's `.oc/lock` included; closing that window leaves the `.oc/lock` in place. `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`: clicking `Cancel` removes the text and the row and opens no window. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher keeps its code.

**Acceptance.** After the read-only offer lands, a picked kit whose lock another holder owns MUST show the holder with Open read-only and Cancel on one row, and Open read-only MUST open the constructor over the kit's read-only context writing nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing` and `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
